<title>HONG KONG: Carr Indosuez sets warrants on red chip basket.</title>
<headline>Carr Indosuez sets warrants on red chip basket.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Carr Indosuez Asia (Derivatives) Ltd said on Thursday it has issued 60 million American-style call warrants on a basket of red chip stocks.</p>
<p>Each basket comprises of:</p>
<p>  China Resources Beijing Land Ltd	0.25 shares</p>
<p>  China Resources Enterprise Ltd	  1    share</p>
<p>  Ng Fung Hong Ltd			    0.50 shares</p>
<p>  Guangnan (Holdings) Ltd		   0.25 shares</p>
<p>  Guangzhou Investment Co Ltd	     0.50 shares</p>
<p>  China Travel International Investment</p>
<p>    Hong Kong Ltd			     0.50 shares</p>
<p>  China Overseas Land &amp; Investment Ltd  1    share</p>
<p>  Cosco Pacific Ltd			   1    share</p>
<p>  Shanghai Industrial Holdings Ltd	0.75 shares</p>
<p>Ten warrants control one basket.</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE	HK$38.5088   PREMIUM	 10.75 PCT</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE	 HK$0.8878    GEARING	 4.82x</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	  14.NOV.97    PAYDATE	 UNAVAILABLE</p>
<p> LISTING	     HONG KONG    MIN EXER LOT  20,000</p>
<p> SPOT REFERENCE    HK$42.7875</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
